---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Erickson Mugendi Nyaga — Data Analyst & Data Scientist</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Portfolio of Erickson Mugendi Nyaga, a data analyst & data scientist: data analytics and business insights, machine learning pipelines and data engineering. I build end-to-end pipelines and ML models that turn raw data into verified business answers."
    />
    <link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 viewBox=%220 0 100 100%22><text y=%22.9em%22 font-size=%2290%22>📊</text></svg>" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="hero">
      <p class="kicker">Erickson Mugendi Nyaga</p>
      <h1>Data Analyst &amp; Data Scientist.<br />I build data pipelines and ML models that turn raw data into verified business answers.</h1>
      <p class="sub">
        Kenya-based and open to remote international work. Every project runs end-to-end — raw data in, verified answer out.
      </p>
      <p class="impact">
        <span>6 featured projects</span>
        <span>3 work personas</span>
        <span>ML · analytics · pipelines</span>
        <span>SQL · Python · Power BI</span>
      </p>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="projects" aria-label="Featured projects">
        <p class="section-tag">Featured projects</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Work that answers real business questions</h2>
        <p class="section-note">
          Six projects drawn from my GitHub, grouped by the work persona they demonstrate. Open any card to see what I did, what it delivered, and where the code lives.
        </p>
        <div class="project-grid">
          {
            features.map((p) => (
              <article class="card">
                <div class="card-head">
                  <p class="tag">{p.tag}</p>
                  <p class="industry">{p.industry}</p>
                </div>
                <h3>{p.title}</h3>
                <p class="metrics">{p.metrics}</p>
                <p class="blurb">{p.blurb}</p>
                <p class="outcome">
                  <span class="arrow">→</span>
                  <span>{p.outcome}</span>
                </p>
                <p class="links">
                  {p.links.map((l) => (
                    <a href={l.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                      {l.label}
                    </a>
                  ))}
                </p>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="projects" aria-label="All projects">
        <p class="section-tag">All projects</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">GitHub projects, grouped by work persona</h2>
        <p class="section-note">
          Six projects drawn from my GitHub, grouped by the work persona they demonstrate. Each links to its repository with a summary you can verify in seconds.
        </p>
        <div class="persona-groups">
          {
            personas.map((p) => (
              <div class="persona-group">
                <p class="tag">{p.name}</p>
                <h3 style:color={p.color}>{p.projects.map((pp) => pp.title).join(" &middot; &middot; &middot; ") || "No projects"}</h3>
                <div class="persona-cards">
                  {
                    p.projects.map((pp) => (
                      <div class="mini-card">
                        <p class="mini-tag">{pp.tag}</p>
                        <p class="mini-title">{pp.title}</p>
                        <p class="mini-blurb">{pp.blurb}</p>
                        <p class="mini-links">
                          {pp.links.map((l) => (
                            <a href={l.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{l.label} →</a>
                          ))}
                        </p>
                      </div>
                    ))
                  }
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="skills" aria-label="Skills">
        <h2>Tools I work with</h2>
        <ul class="skills-grid">
          {
            skills.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)
          }
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="about" aria-label="About">
        <p class="section-tag">About</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">I turn uncertainty into decisions</h2>
        <p>
          I hold a BSc in Applied Optics and Lasers and retrained as a data analyst / data scientist through the LuxDevHQ bootcamp. The physics background shows up in how I work: state the question precisely, measure before claiming, and show the numbers behind every conclusion.
        </p>
        <p>
          My approach is the same for every project: define the business question, clean and shape the data, build the model or pipeline, and verify the result before it leaves my machine. The three projects above are the proof — each one has a documented pipeline, tests guarding its claims, and a README a reviewer can follow without asking me anything.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="contact" aria-label="Contact">
      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:mugendierickson@gmail.com">mugendierickson@gmail.com</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
        <a href="https://github.com/cruqza" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/cruqza</a>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
